---
import SimLayout from '../../../layouts/SimLayout.astro';
---

<SimLayout
  areaSlug="physics"
  title="Ideal Gas"
  description="A few hundred molecules bouncing in a box, and nothing else. Pressure is the drumming of their impacts, temperature is how fast they are, and PV = NkT is not a law you have to be told, it is what the counting adds up to."
>
  <div class="sim">
    <div class="sim-stage">
      <canvas id="gas" class="gas-canvas" width="1000" height="880"></canvas>
    </div>

    <div class="sim-panel">
      <div style="display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap">
        <button class="btn" id="run">Pause</button>
        <button class="btn ghost" id="reset">Reset</button>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Walls</label>
        <div class="seg" id="walls">
          <button data-w="bath" class="active">Held at T</button>
          <button data-w="insulated">Insulated</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Molecules N <b id="nval">300</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="n" min="20" max="600" step="10" value="300" />
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Wall temperature <b id="tval">300 K</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="temp" min="50" max="1200" step="10" value="300" />
        <div class="scale-hint"><span>cold</span><span>hot</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Piston position <b id="vol">27000 nm³</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="piston" min="30" max="100" step="1" value="100" />
        <div class="scale-hint"><span>squeezed</span><span>roomy</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="control">
        <label>Time rate <b id="rateval">1.0×</b></label>
        <input type="range" id="rate" min="10" max="300" step="5" value="100" />
      </div>

      <label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="trail" /> Trace one molecule</label>
      <label class="check"><input type="checkbox" id="hits" checked /> Flash every wall hit</label>

      <div class="readout">
        <div class="row"><span id="l1">Pressure, measured</span><b id="r1">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l2">Pressure, from NkT/V</span><b id="r2">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l3">Temperature</span><b id="r3">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l4">Volume</span><b id="r4">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l5">Root mean square speed</span><b id="r5">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l6">PV / NkT</span><b id="r6">—</b></div>
        <div class="row"><span id="l7">Wall hits</span><b id="r7">—</b></div>
      </div>

      <p style="font-size:.82rem;color:var(--text-faint);margin:0;line-height:1.5">
        A flat gas in a slab 10 nm thick, so every molecule has two directions to
        move in rather than three. Everything else is exactly the real thing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <Fragment slot="observe">
    <li>
      Watch a single wall. Each flash is one molecule turning round, and each one
      delivers a tiny kick. <b>Pressure is nothing but those kicks added up</b>,
      and the measured number next to the box is literally the running total of
      momentum delivered, divided by the area and the time.
    </li>
    <li>
      The measured pressure and NkT/V agree to a few percent, and they were
      never made to. One is counted from impacts, the other is the gas law. Add
      molecules and both climb together, because twice as many molecules means
      twice as many kicks per second. The few percent left over has a name, and
      it is the next thing to look at.
    </li>
    <li>
      Push the piston in with the walls held at a temperature. The molecules keep
      the same speeds but hit a smaller box more often, so the pressure rises as
      1/V. Boyle's law is a bookkeeping statement about how often something
      bounces.
    </li>
    <li>
      Now set the walls to Insulated and push the piston in quickly. The gas
      <b>heats up with nothing heating it</b>. Look closely at the moving wall:
      a molecule bouncing off an advancing piston comes back faster, exactly like
      a ball off a swung bat. That is all adiabatic heating has ever been.
    </li>
    <li>
      Pull the piston back out while insulated and the gas cools, for the mirror
      reason. On the P-V plot the path is steeper than the isotherm through the
      same point, which is the whole content of PV<sup>γ</sup> = constant.
    </li>
    <li>
      Start every molecule at the same speed with Reset, then watch the speed
      histogram. Collisions alone, with no rule about distributions anywhere in
      the code, smear it into the <b>Maxwell-Boltzmann</b> curve drawn over it,
      and it stays there. Equilibrium is not imposed, it is what shuffling does.
    </li>
    <li>
      Raise the wall temperature and watch the histogram slide right and flatten.
      There is no such thing as the speed of a molecule at 500 K, only a spread,
      and the tail of that spread is what boils, evaporates and reacts.
    </li>
    <li>
      Crowd the box: raise N and squeeze the piston at the same time. PV/NkT
      creeps above one and keeps climbing. Nothing broke, the law did: a real
      molecule takes up room, so the space left for the others is less than the
      volume you measured. That correction is the <b>b</b> in van der Waals, and
      it is the first thing that stops a gas from being ideal.
    </li>
    <li>
      Turn on the trace and follow one molecule for a while. It goes nowhere in
      particular, at hundreds of metres per second, changing direction constantly.
      The gas is calm because a few hundred of these average out, not because
      anything in it is calm.
    </li>
  </Fragment>
</SimLayout>

<script>
  import { setupCanvas, makeText, subHtml } from '../../../lib/sim';

  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  // Hard disks in a box, nothing more. Nitrogen mass, real speeds, nanometre
  // box: the numbers on screen are the numbers a real gas would give.
  // ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  const KB = 1.380649e-23; // J/K
  const MASS = 4.65e-26; // kg, one N2 molecule
  const DEPTH = 10e-9; // the slab is this thick, which turns area into volume
  const BOX_W = 60e-9, BOX_H = 45e-9; // metres
  const RADIUS = 0.28e-9; // real collision size, dilute enough to stay ideal
  // The piston follows the slider live, but its velocity is ramped rather than
  // switched, so the gas never sees a discontinuity. Above roughly a third of
  // the molecular speed the compression stops being quasi-static and starts
  // being a shock, which the scene says out loud when it happens.
  const PISTON_MAX = 260; // m/s
  const PISTON_CHASE = 40e-12; // seconds of gas time to close the gap
  const PISTON_SMOOTH = 1.6e-12; // how long the velocity takes to change

  const state = {
    n: 300,
    temp: 300, // wall temperature, K
    piston: 1, // fraction of the box the piston leaves
    walls: 'bath' as 'bath' | 'insulated',
    rate: 1,
    running: true,
    trail: false,
    hits: true,
  };

  type P = { x: number; y: number; vx: number; vy: number };
  let parts: P[] = [];
  let pistonX = BOX_W; // metres
  let pistonV = 0; // metres per second, from the slider being dragged
  let impulse = 0; // momentum delivered to the walls since the last window
  let window_ = 0; // seconds that impulse has been accumulating over
  let pressure = 0; // Pa, from the impacts
  let pFast = 0; // a quick average, for while the piston is moving
  let cumImp = 0, cumT = 0; // the long average, which is what a gauge reads
  let hitCount = 0;
  let simTime = 0;
  type Flash = { x: number; y: number; life: number };
  let flashes: Flash[] = [];
  let trail: { x: number; y: number }[] = [];
  type PVPoint = { v: number; p: number };
  let pvPath: PVPoint[] = [];
  // Where the gas was when the piston last stood still: the curves in the P-V
  // panel are drawn through this, so a moving path can be compared with them.
  let ref = { v: 0, p: 0, T: 300 };

  const volume = () => pistonX * BOX_H * DEPTH; // m³
  const area = () => pistonX * BOX_H;

  /** Temperature straight from the molecules: in 2D, mean KE = kT. */
  function temperature() {
    if (!parts.length) return 0;
    let s = 0;
    for (const p of parts) s += p.vx * p.vx + p.vy * p.vy;
    return (MASS * (s / parts.length)) / (2 * KB);
  }
  const vThermal = (T: number) => Math.sqrt((2 * KB * T) / MASS);

  function build() {
    parts = [];
    pistonX = BOX_W * state.piston;
    // Everyone starts with the same speed, so the spread that appears later
    // can only have come from the collisions.
    const v0 = vThermal(state.temp);
    for (let i = 0; i < state.n; i++) {
      const a = Math.random() * Math.PI * 2;
      parts.push({
        x: RADIUS + Math.random() * (pistonX - 2 * RADIUS),
        y: RADIUS + Math.random() * (BOX_H - 2 * RADIUS),
        vx: Math.cos(a) * v0,
        vy: Math.sin(a) * v0,
      });
    }
    impulse = 0;
    window_ = 0;
    pressure = 0;
    pFast = 0;
    cumImp = 0;
    cumT = 0;
    hitCount = 0;
    simTime = 0;
    flashes = [];
    trail = [];
    pvPath = [];
  }

  function flash(x: number, y: number) {
    if (!state.hits) return;
    flashes.push({ x, y, life: 1 });
    if (flashes.length > 60) flashes.shift();
  }

  /** A standard normal, for the tangential kick a hot wall gives. */
  function gauss() {
    let u = 0, v = 0;
    while (u === 0) u = Math.random();
    while (v === 0) v = Math.random();
    return Math.sqrt(-2 * Math.log(u)) * Math.cos(2 * Math.PI * v);
  }

  /**
   * A wall in a heat bath forgets what hit it and hands back a fresh molecule
   * drawn from the wall's own temperature. The normal component has to be
   * flux weighted (fast molecules leave more often, p ∝ v e^(−mv²/2kT)) while
   * the tangential one is plain Gaussian. Getting that weighting wrong makes
   * the wall quietly cool or heat the gas it is supposed to be holding steady.
   */
  function wallBounce(p: P, axis: 'x' | 'y', sign: number) {
    if (state.walls === 'bath') {
      const vp = Math.sqrt((KB * state.temp) / MASS); // kT/m, one dimension
      const vn = vp * Math.sqrt(-2 * Math.log(1 - Math.random() * 0.999999));
      const vt = vp * gauss();
      if (axis === 'x') {
        p.vx = sign * vn;
        p.vy = vt;
      } else {
        p.vy = sign * vn;
        p.vx = vt;
      }
    } else {
      if (axis === 'x') p.vx = sign * Math.abs(p.vx);
      else p.vy = sign * Math.abs(p.vy);
    }
  }

  function step(dt: number) {
    // Follow the slider, but through a rate limit and then a velocity ramp, so
    // however fast the slider is thrown the wall itself always accelerates
    // smoothly and no molecule is ever teleported through it.
    const targetPiston = BOX_W * state.piston;
    const desired = Math.max(
      -PISTON_MAX,
      Math.min(PISTON_MAX, (targetPiston - pistonX) / PISTON_CHASE)
    );
    pistonV += (desired - pistonV) * Math.min(1, dt / PISTON_SMOOTH);
    // Snap the last fraction of a nanometre so the wall genuinely comes to rest
    // and the long pressure average has something steady to average over.
    if (Math.abs(targetPiston - pistonX) < 5e-11) {
      pistonX = targetPiston;
      pistonV = 0;
    }
    let stepMove = pistonV * dt;
    // never overshoot the slider
    const gap = targetPiston - pistonX;
    if (Math.abs(stepMove) > Math.abs(gap)) {
      stepMove = gap;
      pistonV = dt > 0 ? gap / dt : 0;
    }
    pistonX += stepMove;
    // keep every molecule on the gas side of the wall, however fast it moved
    for (const p of parts) if (p.x > pistonX - RADIUS) p.x = pistonX - RADIUS;

    for (const p of parts) {
      p.x += p.vx * dt;
      p.y += p.vy * dt;

      // Every bounce below books the momentum actually handed to the wall,
      // m|Δv|, rather than assuming a mirror reflection. With a thermostat the
      // molecule leaves at a different speed than it arrived, and assuming
      // otherwise inflates the measured pressure by half.
      if (p.x < RADIUS) {
        p.x = RADIUS;
        const before = p.vx;
        wallBounce(p, 'x', 1);
        impulse += MASS * Math.abs(p.vx - before);
        hitCount++;
        flash(0, p.y);
      } else if (p.x > pistonX - RADIUS) {
        p.x = pistonX - RADIUS;
        const before = p.vx;
        const u = pistonV;
        // Bouncing off a moving wall: reflect in the wall's own frame, which
        // is exactly why squeezing a gas heats it.
        if (state.walls === 'insulated') p.vx = 2 * u - p.vx;
        else {
          wallBounce(p, 'x', -1);
          p.vx += u;
        }
        impulse += MASS * Math.abs(p.vx - before);
        hitCount++;
        flash(pistonX, p.y);
      }
      if (p.y < RADIUS) {
        p.y = RADIUS;
        const before = p.vy;
        wallBounce(p, 'y', 1);
        impulse += MASS * Math.abs(p.vy - before);
        hitCount++;
        flash(p.x, 0);
      } else if (p.y > BOX_H - RADIUS) {
        p.y = BOX_H - RADIUS;
        const before = p.vy;
        wallBounce(p, 'y', -1);
        impulse += MASS * Math.abs(p.vy - before);
        hitCount++;
        flash(p.x, BOX_H);
      }
    }

    collide();

    window_ += dt;
    simTime += dt;
    if (Math.abs(pistonV) < 1e-6 && pressure > 0) ref = { v: volume(), p: pressure, T: temperature() };
    if (state.trail && parts.length) {
      trail.push({ x: parts[0].x, y: parts[0].y });
      if (trail.length > 900) trail.shift();
    }
    for (let k = flashes.length - 1; k >= 0; k--) {
      flashes[k].life -= dt * 4e12;
      if (flashes[k].life <= 0) flashes.splice(k, 1);
    }
  }

  /** Elastic hard-disk collisions, found with a grid so N can be large. */
  function collide() {
    const cell = RADIUS * 3;
    const cols = Math.max(1, Math.ceil(pistonX / cell));
    const rows = Math.max(1, Math.ceil(BOX_H / cell));
    const grid: number[][] = new Array(cols * rows);
    for (let i = 0; i < parts.length; i++) {
      const c = Math.min(cols - 1, Math.max(0, Math.floor(parts[i].x / cell)));
      const r = Math.min(rows - 1, Math.max(0, Math.floor(parts[i].y / cell)));
      const k = r * cols + c;
      (grid[k] ||= []).push(i);
    }
    const d2 = (2 * RADIUS) * (2 * RADIUS);
    for (let r = 0; r < rows; r++)
      for (let c = 0; c < cols; c++) {
        const here = grid[r * cols + c];
        if (!here) continue;
        for (let dr = 0; dr <= 1; dr++)
          for (let dc = -1; dc <= 1; dc++) {
            if (dr === 0 && dc < 0) continue;
            const rr = r + dr, cc = c + dc;
            if (rr >= rows || cc < 0 || cc >= cols) continue;
            const there = grid[rr * cols + cc];
            if (!there) continue;
            for (const i of here)
              for (const j of there) {
                if (j <= i) continue;
                const a = parts[i], b = parts[j];
                const dx = b.x - a.x, dy = b.y - a.y;
                const dist2 = dx * dx + dy * dy;
                if (dist2 > d2 || dist2 === 0) continue;
                const dist = Math.sqrt(dist2);
                const nx = dx / dist, ny = dy / dist;
                const dvx = b.vx - a.vx, dvy = b.vy - a.vy;
                const rel = dvx * nx + dvy * ny;
                if (rel > 0) continue; // already separating
                // equal masses: they simply swap the normal component
                a.vx += rel * nx;
                a.vy += rel * ny;
                b.vx -= rel * nx;
                b.vy -= rel * ny;
                const push = (2 * RADIUS - dist) / 2;
                a.x -= nx * push;
                a.y -= ny * push;
                b.x += nx * push;
                b.y += ny * push;
              }
          }
      }
  }

  // --- formatting ------------------------------------------------------------

  function eng(x: number, unit: string, digits = 2): string {
    const a = Math.abs(x);
    if (a === 0) return `0 ${unit}`;
    const steps: [number, string][] = [
      [1e-24, 'y'], [1e-21, 'z'], [1e-18, 'a'], [1e-15, 'f'],
      [1e-12, 'p'], [1e-9, 'n'], [1e-6, 'µ'], [1e-3, 'm'],
      [1, ''], [1e3, 'k'], [1e6, 'M'], [1e9, 'G'],
    ];
    let pick = steps[0];
    for (const s of steps) if (a >= s[0]) pick = s;
    return `${(x / pick[0]).toFixed(digits)} ${pick[1]}${unit}`;
  }
  const nm3 = (v: number) => `${(v * 1e27).toFixed(0)} nm³`;

  // --- canvas ----------------------------------------------------------------

  const canvas = document.getElementById('gas') as HTMLCanvasElement;
  const { ctx, W, H } = setupCanvas(canvas, () => draw());
  const cssVar = (n: string) => getComputedStyle(canvas).getPropertyValue(n).trim();
  const inkRGB = () => cssVar('--stage-ink') || '232,233,236';
  const inkA = (a: number) => `rgba(${inkRGB()},${a})`;
  const bg = () => cssVar('--stage-bg') || '#0d0e12';
  const { label, textWidth } = makeText(ctx, inkA);

  const COOL = '#5b8cff';
  const HOT = '#f9736a';
  const ACC = '#7c8cff';
  const WARM = '#f59e0b';
  const GREEN = '#34d399';
  const BAD_RED = '#ef4444';

  const BOX = { x: 20, y: 86, w: 640, h: 560 };
  const HIST = { x: 680, y: 86, w: 300, h: 280 };
  const PV = { x: 680, y: 406, w: 300, h: 240 };
  const NOTE = { x: 20, y: 686, w: 960, h: 174 };

  function rr(x: number, y: number, w: number, h: number, r: number) {
    const rad = Math.min(r, Math.abs(w) / 2, Math.abs(h) / 2);
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x + rad, y);
    ctx.lineTo(x + w - rad, y);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x + w, y, x + w, y + rad);
    ctx.lineTo(x + w, y + h - rad);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x + w, y + h, x + w - rad, y + h);
    ctx.lineTo(x + rad, y + h);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x, y + h, x, y + h - rad);
    ctx.lineTo(x, y + rad);
    ctx.quadraticCurveTo(x, y, x + rad, y);
    ctx.closePath();
  }
  function panel(p: { x: number; y: number; w: number; h: number }, title: string) {
    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.1);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    rr(p.x, p.y, p.w, p.h, 10);
    ctx.stroke();
    label(title, p.x + 2, p.y - 9, 0.5, 'left', 11);
  }
  function arrow(x1: number, y1: number, x2: number, y2: number, size = 5) {
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x1, y1);
    ctx.lineTo(x2, y2);
    ctx.stroke();
    const a = Math.atan2(y2 - y1, x2 - x1);
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(x2, y2);
    ctx.lineTo(x2 - size * Math.cos(a - 0.4), y2 - size * Math.sin(a - 0.4));
    ctx.lineTo(x2 - size * Math.cos(a + 0.4), y2 - size * Math.sin(a + 0.4));
    ctx.closePath();
    ctx.fill();
  }

  // --- the box ---------------------------------------------------------------

  const inner = () => ({
    x: BOX.x + 46,
    y: BOX.y + 54,
    w: BOX.w - 92,
    h: BOX.h - 130,
  });
  const SX = (x: number) => inner().x + (x / BOX_W) * inner().w;
  const SY = (y: number) => inner().y + (y / BOX_H) * inner().h;

  function speedColour(v: number, vref: number) {
    const f = Math.max(0, Math.min(1, (v / (vref * 1.35)) ** 1.6));
    const r = Math.round(91 + f * (249 - 91));
    const g = Math.round(140 + f * (115 - 140));
    const b = Math.round(255 + f * (106 - 255));
    return `rgb(${r},${g},${b})`;
  }

  function drawBox() {
    panel(BOX, 'THE GAS ITSELF');
    const b = inner();
    const px = SX(pistonX);
    const T = temperature();
    const vref = vThermal(state.temp);

    ctx.fillStyle = inkA(0.03);
    ctx.fillRect(b.x, b.y, px - b.x, b.h);
    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.28);
    ctx.lineWidth = 2;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(px, b.y);
    ctx.lineTo(b.x, b.y);
    ctx.lineTo(b.x, b.y + b.h);
    ctx.lineTo(px, b.y + b.h);
    ctx.stroke();

    // the piston, with a handle so it reads as the thing you are pushing
    ctx.fillStyle = inkA(0.32);
    rr(px, b.y - 6, 16, b.h + 12, 3);
    ctx.fill();
    ctx.fillStyle = inkA(0.18);
    ctx.fillRect(px + 16, b.y + b.h / 2 - 5, 26, 10);
    if (Math.abs(pistonV) > 1) {
      ctx.strokeStyle = WARM;
      ctx.fillStyle = WARM;
      ctx.lineWidth = 2;
      const dir = Math.sign(pistonV);
      arrow(px + 52, b.y + b.h / 2, px + 52 + dir * 30, b.y + b.h / 2, 7);
      const vrms = Math.sqrt((2 * KB * temperature()) / MASS);
      // Past roughly the sound speed a squeeze piles up into a shock rather
      // than compressing the gas evenly.
      const shock = Math.abs(pistonV) > 0.45 * vrms;
      const cap = shock ? 'too fast: shock' : pistonV < 0 ? 'squeezing' : 'expanding';
      const room = BOX.x + BOX.w - 12 - (px + 24);
      const fits = textWidth(cap, 12) < room;
      label(cap, fits ? px + 24 : px - 14, b.y + b.h / 2 - 12, 0.85, fits ? 'left' : 'right', 12, shock ? BAD_RED : WARM);
    }

    if (state.trail && trail.length > 1) {
      ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.28);
      ctx.lineWidth = 1;
      ctx.beginPath();
      trail.forEach((p, k) => (k ? ctx.lineTo(SX(p.x), SY(p.y)) : ctx.moveTo(SX(p.x), SY(p.y))));
      ctx.stroke();
    }

    const rpx = Math.max(3, (RADIUS / BOX_W) * b.w);
    for (let i = 0; i < parts.length; i++) {
      const p = parts[i];
      const v = Math.hypot(p.vx, p.vy);
      ctx.fillStyle = speedColour(v, vref);
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(SX(p.x), SY(p.y), rpx, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
    }
    if (state.trail && parts.length) {
      ctx.strokeStyle = '#fff';
      ctx.lineWidth = 2;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(SX(parts[0].x), SY(parts[0].y), rpx + 3, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.stroke();
    }

    for (const f of flashes) {
      const a = Math.max(0, f.life);
      ctx.strokeStyle = `rgba(245,158,11,${a * 0.9})`;
      ctx.lineWidth = 2;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(SX(f.x), SY(f.y), 3 + (1 - a) * 9, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.stroke();
    }

    label(`T = ${T.toFixed(0)} K`, b.x, b.y - 16, 0.85, 'left', 14, HOT);
    label(`P = ${eng(pressure, 'Pa', 2)}`, b.x + 190, b.y - 16, 0.85, 'left', 14, WARM);
    label(`V = ${nm3(volume())}`, b.x + 400, b.y - 16, 0.85, 'left', 14, ACC);

    // the pressure gauge: impacts turning into a number
    const gy = b.y + b.h + 30;
    const pmax = Math.max(1e5, pressure * 1.4);
    label('pressure', b.x, gy + 12, 0.5, 'left', 11);
    ctx.fillStyle = inkA(0.07);
    rr(b.x + 90, gy, b.w - 90, 16, 4);
    ctx.fill();
    ctx.fillStyle = WARM;
    rr(b.x + 90, gy, Math.max(2, (pressure / pmax) * (b.w - 90)), 16, 4);
    ctx.fill();
    label(eng(pressure, 'Pa', 2), b.x + b.w - 8, gy + 12, 0.8, 'right', 11);
  }

  // --- speed histogram -------------------------------------------------------

  function drawHist() {
    panel(HIST, 'HOW FAST THEY ARE');
    const px = HIST.x + 40, py = HIST.y + 26, pw = HIST.w - 58, ph = HIST.h - 66;
    const T = Math.max(1, temperature());
    const vmax = vThermal(Math.max(state.temp, T)) * 2.6;
    const NB = 26;
    const bins = new Array(NB).fill(0);
    for (const p of parts) {
      const v = Math.hypot(p.vx, p.vy);
      const k = Math.floor((v / vmax) * NB);
      if (k >= 0 && k < NB) bins[k]++;
    }
    const top = Math.max(1, ...bins);
    for (let k = 0; k < NB; k++) {
      const x = px + (k * pw) / NB;
      const h = (bins[k] / top) * ph;
      ctx.fillStyle = speedColour(((k + 0.5) / NB) * vmax, vThermal(state.temp));
      ctx.globalAlpha = 0.75;
      ctx.fillRect(x + 1, py + ph - h, pw / NB - 2, h);
      ctx.globalAlpha = 1;
    }
    // Maxwell-Boltzmann in two dimensions: f(v) ∝ v exp(−mv²/2kT)
    ctx.strokeStyle = GREEN;
    ctx.lineWidth = 2;
    ctx.beginPath();
    let fmax = 0;
    const f = (v: number) => v * Math.exp((-MASS * v * v) / (2 * KB * T));
    for (let k = 0; k <= 120; k++) fmax = Math.max(fmax, f((k / 120) * vmax));
    for (let k = 0; k <= 120; k++) {
      const v = (k / 120) * vmax;
      const y = py + ph - (f(v) / fmax) * ph * (top / Math.max(top, 1));
      k ? ctx.lineTo(px + (v / vmax) * pw, y) : ctx.moveTo(px + (v / vmax) * pw, y);
    }
    ctx.stroke();

    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.2);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(px, py);
    ctx.lineTo(px, py + ph);
    ctx.lineTo(px + pw, py + ph);
    ctx.stroke();
    label('0', px, py + ph + 16, 0.35, 'center', 10);
    label(`${(vmax).toFixed(0)} m/s`, px + pw, py + ph + 16, 0.35, 'right', 10);
    label('Maxwell-Boltzmann', px + pw, py + 12, 0.8, 'right', 10, GREEN);
    label('nobody wrote this curve into the code', px, HIST.y + HIST.h - 14, 0.4, 'left', 10);
  }

  // --- P-V diagram -----------------------------------------------------------

  function drawPV() {
    panel(PV, 'WHERE THE GAS IS, ON A P-V PLOT');
    const px = PV.x + 54, py = PV.y + 22, pw = PV.w - 74, ph = PV.h - 62;
    const vmin = BOX_W * 0.28 * BOX_H * DEPTH, vmax = BOX_W * BOX_H * DEPTH * 1.06;
    const N = parts.length;
    const pAt = (v: number, T: number) => (N * KB * T) / v;
    const pmax = Math.max(pAt(vmin, Math.max(state.temp, temperature())) * 0.75, 1e5);
    const X = (v: number) => px + ((v - vmin) / (vmax - vmin)) * pw;
    const Y = (p: number) => py + ph - Math.min(1, p / pmax) * ph;

    ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.2);
    ctx.lineWidth = 1;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.moveTo(px, py);
    ctx.lineTo(px, py + ph);
    ctx.lineTo(px + pw, py + ph);
    ctx.stroke();

    // a few isotherms for scale
    for (const T of [150, 300, 600, 1000]) {
      ctx.strokeStyle = inkA(0.14);
      ctx.beginPath();
      for (let k = 0; k <= 60; k++) {
        const v = vmin + ((vmax - vmin) * k) / 60;
        k ? ctx.lineTo(X(v), Y(pAt(v, T))) : ctx.moveTo(X(v), Y(pAt(v, T)));
      }
      ctx.stroke();
    }

    // From where the piston last rested: the isotherm you would follow with the
    // walls held at a temperature, and the adiabat you would follow insulated.
    // In two dimensions γ = 2.
    const v0 = ref.v > 0 ? ref.v : volume(), p0 = ref.p > 0 ? ref.p : pressure;
    for (const [gamma, col] of [[1, 'rgba(124,140,255,0.6)'], [2, 'rgba(245,158,11,0.6)']] as [number, string][]) {
      ctx.strokeStyle = col;
      ctx.setLineDash(gamma === 2 ? [5, 4] : [2, 4]);
      ctx.lineWidth = 1.5;
      ctx.beginPath();
      for (let k = 0; k <= 60; k++) {
        const v = vmin + ((vmax - vmin) * k) / 60;
        const p = p0 * Math.pow(v0 / v, gamma);
        k ? ctx.lineTo(X(v), Y(p)) : ctx.moveTo(X(v), Y(p));
      }
      ctx.stroke();
    }
    ctx.setLineDash([]);

    if (pvPath.length > 1) {
      ctx.strokeStyle = GREEN;
      ctx.lineWidth = 1.6;
      ctx.beginPath();
      pvPath.forEach((q, k) => (k ? ctx.lineTo(X(q.v), Y(q.p)) : ctx.moveTo(X(q.v), Y(q.p))));
      ctx.stroke();
    }
    ctx.fillStyle = GREEN;
    ctx.beginPath();
    ctx.arc(X(volume()), Y(pressure), 5, 0, Math.PI * 2);
    ctx.fill();

    label('V', px + pw, py + ph + 16, 0.4, 'right', 10);
    label('P', px - 8, py + 8, 0.4, 'right', 10);
    label('isotherm from here', px + 6, py + 12, 0.55, 'left', 10, ACC);
    label('adiabat from here', px + 6, py + 26, 0.55, 'left', 10, WARM);
    label('the path you take', px + 6, py + 40, 0.55, 'left', 10, GREEN);
  }

  // --- the explainer strip ---------------------------------------------------

  function drawNote() {
    panel(NOTE, 'WHAT PRESSURE ACTUALLY IS');
    const T = temperature();
    const N = parts.length;
    const pLaw = (N * KB * T) / volume();
    const x0 = NOTE.x + 28;

    label('one molecule hits a wall', x0, NOTE.y + 34, 0.6, 'left', 13, HOT);
    label('it turns round, so its momentum changes by 2mv', x0, NOTE.y + 56, 0.45, 'left', 11);
    label('add every hit over a while, divide by area and time', x0, NOTE.y + 78, 0.45, 'left', 11);
    label(`${hitCount.toLocaleString()} hits counted so far`, x0, NOTE.y + 100, 0.55, 'left', 11, WARM);

    const mx = NOTE.x + 400;
    label('measured from the impacts', mx, NOTE.y + 34, 0.6, 'left', 13, WARM);
    label(eng(pressure, 'Pa', 3), mx, NOTE.y + 62, 0.9, 'left', 16, WARM);
    label('what the gas law says', mx, NOTE.y + 96, 0.6, 'left', 13, ACC);
    label(eng(pLaw, 'Pa', 3), mx, NOTE.y + 124, 0.9, 'left', 16, ACC);

    const ratio = pLaw > 0 ? pressure / pLaw : 0;
    const rx = NOTE.x + 700;
    label('P V / N k T', rx, NOTE.y + 34, 0.6, 'left', 13, GREEN);
    label(ratio.toFixed(3), rx, NOTE.y + 68, 0.95, 'left', 22, GREEN);
    label('nothing forces these to agree,', rx, NOTE.y + 96, 0.42, 'left', 11);
    label('one is counted and one is derived', rx, NOTE.y + 112, 0.42, 'left', 11);
    // Only worth naming once the gas has settled: while the piston is moving
    // the gauge is chasing a moving target and the gap means nothing.
    if (Math.abs(pistonV) > 1)
      label('the piston is moving, let it settle', rx, NOTE.y + 132, 0.5, 'left', 11, WARM);
    else if (ratio > 1.02)
      label(
        `the extra ${((ratio - 1) * 100).toFixed(0)}% is the room the molecules themselves take up`,
        rx,
        NOTE.y + 132,
        0.5,
        'left',
        11,
        WARM
      );

    label(
      `each molecule carries kT on average: at ${T.toFixed(0)} K that is ${eng(KB * T, 'J', 1)}, or ${(((KB * T) / 1.602e-19) * 1000).toFixed(1)} meV`,
      x0,
      NOTE.y + NOTE.h - 18,
      0.4,
      'left',
      11
    );
  }

  // --- readouts --------------------------------------------------------------

  const el = (id: string) => document.getElementById(id) as HTMLElement;
  const setRow = (n: number, lab: string, val: string) => {
    el('l' + n).innerHTML = subHtml(lab);
    el('r' + n).textContent = val;
  };
  function updateReadout() {
    const T = temperature();
    const N = parts.length;
    const pLaw = (N * KB * T) / volume();
    setRow(1, 'Pressure, measured', eng(pressure, 'Pa', 2));
    setRow(2, 'Pressure, from NkT/V', eng(pLaw, 'Pa', 2));
    setRow(3, 'Temperature', `${T.toFixed(1)} K`);
    setRow(4, 'Volume', nm3(volume()));
    setRow(5, 'Speed v_rms', `${Math.sqrt((2 * KB * T) / MASS).toFixed(0)} m/s`);
    setRow(6, 'PV / NkT', pLaw > 0 ? (pressure / pLaw).toFixed(3) : '—');
    setRow(7, 'Wall hits', hitCount.toLocaleString());
  }

  // --- loop ------------------------------------------------------------------

  function draw() {
    ctx.clearRect(0, 0, W, H);
    label('Ideal Gas', 20, 30, 0.85, 'left', 14);
    label(
      state.walls === 'bath'
        ? 'the walls hold the temperature, so squeezing is isothermal'
        : 'insulated: the only way in or out for energy is the piston',
      20,
      52,
      0.5,
      'left',
      11,
      GREEN
    );
    const legend: [string, string][] = [
      [COOL, 'slow'],
      [HOT, 'fast'],
      [WARM, 'wall hit'],
    ];
    let x = W - 20;
    for (let k = legend.length - 1; k >= 0; k--) {
      const [c, tx] = legend[k];
      const tw = textWidth(tx, 11);
      label(tx, x, 30, 0.55, 'right', 11);
      ctx.fillStyle = c;
      ctx.beginPath();
      ctx.arc(x - tw - 11, 26, 5, 0, Math.PI * 2);
      ctx.fill();
      x -= tw + 30;
    }
    drawBox();
    drawHist();
    drawPV();
    drawNote();
  }

  let last = performance.now();
  let pvClock = 0;
  function frame(now: number) {
    let dtReal = (now - last) / 1000;
    last = now;
    dtReal = Math.min(0.05, Math.max(0, dtReal));
    if (state.running) {
      // Molecules cross the box in about a tenth of a nanosecond, so gas time
      // runs at roughly 30 ps per second of screen time.
      const dt = 8e-14 * state.rate;
      const steps = Math.min(12, Math.max(1, Math.round(dtReal / 0.004)));
      for (let s = 0; s < steps; s++) step(dt);
      // Pressure is the impulse rate over the wall area. A handful of hits per
      // frame is a very noisy number, so it is averaged over about a second of
      // watching: that is what a real gauge does too.
      if (window_ > 0) {
        const wallLen = 2 * (pistonX + BOX_H) * DEPTH;
        const rate = impulse / (window_ * wallLen);
        pFast = pFast === 0 ? rate : pFast * 0.96 + rate * 0.04;
        // A few hundred hits is a noisy sample. Once the piston is still, the
        // average runs over everything since it stopped, which is what a real
        // gauge does and what makes PV/NkT settle down.
        if (Math.abs(pistonV) > 1e-6) {
          cumImp = 0;
          cumT = 0;
          pressure = pFast;
        } else {
          cumImp += impulse;
          cumT += window_;
          pressure = cumT > 0 ? cumImp / (cumT * wallLen) : pFast;
        }
        impulse = 0;
        window_ = 0;
      }
      pvClock += dtReal;
      if (pvClock > 0.08) {
        pvClock = 0;
        pvPath.push({ v: volume(), p: pressure });
        if (pvPath.length > 260) pvPath.shift();
      }
    }
    draw();
    updateReadout();
    requestAnimationFrame(frame);
  }

  // --- controls --------------------------------------------------------------

  const runBtn = el('run');
  runBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
    state.running = !state.running;
    runBtn.textContent = state.running ? 'Pause' : 'Run';
  });
  el('reset').addEventListener('click', build);

  function bindRange(id: string, apply: (n: number) => void, rebuild = false) {
    const inp = el(id) as HTMLInputElement;
    const run = () => {
      apply(+inp.value);
      if (rebuild) build();
    };
    inp.addEventListener('input', run);
    apply(+inp.value);
  }
  bindRange('n', (n) => {
    state.n = n;
    el('nval').textContent = String(n);
  }, true);
  bindRange('temp', (n) => {
    state.temp = n;
    el('tval').textContent = `${n} K`;
    cumImp = 0;
    cumT = 0;
  });
  bindRange('piston', (n) => {
    state.piston = n / 100;
    el('vol').textContent = nm3(BOX_W * state.piston * BOX_H * DEPTH);
  });
  bindRange('rate', (n) => {
    state.rate = n / 100;
    el('rateval').textContent = `${state.rate.toFixed(1)}×`;
  });
  (el('trail') as HTMLInputElement).addEventListener('change', (e) => {
    state.trail = (e.target as HTMLInputElement).checked;
    trail = [];
  });
  (el('hits') as HTMLInputElement).addEventListener('change', (e) => {
    state.hits = (e.target as HTMLInputElement).checked;
  });
  el('walls').addEventListener('click', (e) => {
    const btn = (e.target as HTMLElement).closest('button');
    if (!btn) return;
    document.querySelectorAll('#walls button').forEach((b) => b.classList.remove('active'));
    btn.classList.add('active');
    state.walls = btn.dataset.w as 'bath' | 'insulated';
    pvPath = [];
    cumImp = 0;
    cumT = 0;
  });

  build();
  requestAnimationFrame(frame);
</script>

<style>
  .gas-canvas {
    touch-action: none;
  }
  .scale-hint {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    color: var(--text-faint);
    margin-top: 3px;
  }
  .check {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }
  .check input {
    accent-color: var(--accent);
  }
</style>
